  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A cold front passes through the region this \nmorning and cooler and drier air builds into the region.\n\nThe initial cold front is well offshore, and a secondary cold \nfront will pass through the region early this morning. An upper \nlevel low over the Great Lakes will lift to the northeast, and\nlow pressure will meander over the Canadian Maritimes through\nthe weekend. Meanwhile, surface high pressure builds to the\nsouth and west.\n\nOnce the secondary cold front moves through the region this\nmorning, a tight pressure gradient forms between low pressure to\nthe north and east and high pressure to the south and west.\nNorthwest winds will increase to 15 to 20 mph with 25 to 30 mph\ngusts this afternoon. Much cooler and drier with highs in the\n50s to low 60s and dew points in the 30s to low 40s.\n\nHeading into the second half of the weekend, the upper-level \nlow departs to the north and east as shortwave ridging moves in.\nThe pressure gradient also relaxes some as the surface low pull\nfarther away into Atlantic Canada. This will result in a \nlighter breeze with slightly warmer temperatures compared to \nSaturday and a mainly clear to partly cloudy sky. Expect highs \nSunday mainly in the low 60s following morning lows mainly \nranging from the upper 30s to mid 40s. \n\nGenerally dry and fair weather looks to dominate for early through \nmid next week.",
